{
  "id": "COMPOUND:34435 - PROTEIN:4668",
  "verbalization": "Ent-Gloeosteretriol is implicated in the regulation of Ephrin type-A receptor 8 through a multi-step mechanism involving the Solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 2A1. This transporter is a target of K-252a and Theasaponin E1, both of which are known to modulate the activity of Ephrin type-A receptors. The observed evidence suggests that Ent-Gloeosteretriol may act as a modulator of the Solute carrier organic anion transporter family member 2A1, which in turn influences Ephrin type-A receptor 8 through a pathway involving Theasaponin E1. The integration of these targets highlights a potential role for Ent-Gloeosteretriol in regulating Ephrin type-A receptor 8 via a complex network of interactions, possibly through the modulation of anion transport and receptor signaling. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Ent-Gloeosteretriol and Ephrin type-A receptor 8, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
